<title>ISRAEL: Israel Corp names chairman, manager.</title>
<headline>Israel Corp names chairman, manager.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of directors of the Israel Corp on Sunday appointed Erwin Eisenberg as chairman, replacing his father Shoul Eisenberg who died last month.</p>
<p>Doron Steiger, 39, former deputy managing director of the Dovrat-Shrem investment company, replaced Erwin Eisenberg as general manager, effective May 1, the board said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Israel Corp is one of the major holding companies operating in Israel with investments in over 80 leading companies, including Israel Chemicals.</p>
<p>Billionaire Shoul Eisenberg died of a heart attack in Beijing on March 27.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
